# robotparts' actuator models on BAM's rack: the pivot first, then the leaderboard and the parameters, one file of
# configuration over one data file (models.json: kind model | run | term; each view filters to its kind).
# Every tab opens with its answer (intro: KPI cards; its text is the tab's About note), rolls up across actuators by default (rollup:),
# and links each model to its page (open: side, url: page -> the robotparts-model case). CONTRACT §16; property types
# (status pills, coloured rungs, run-count bars, header icons and tooltips) CONTRACT §28.
# Check it: node bin/data-ui.mjs check <this file>
data: models.json
open: { mode: side, url: page }
facets:
  - actuator
  - rung
  - family
  - { property: benches, label: Bench }
properties:
  actuator: { displayName: Actuator, icon: gauge }
  variant: { displayName: Model, icon: cpu }
  model: { displayName: Model kind, icon: layers }
  rung: { displayName: Rung, type: select, description: "The model ladder's rung (M0 ideal → M5 motor)", options: { M0: gray, M1: brown, M2: blue, M3: purple, M4: green, M5: orange, driver: pink } }
  family: { displayName: Family, type: select }
  ladder_step: { displayName: Ladder step }
  leader: { displayName: Best model }
  headline_x: { displayName: Held-out error, icon: target, description: "The median error on the Oct 23 held-out tapes, in multiples of that actuator's measurement floor: 1 × is as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×" }
  headline_mrad: { displayName: Held-out q RMS }
  dataset_x: { displayName: Dataset, description: "The Oct 24 dataset, in multiples of that actuator's measurement floor: 1 × is as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×" }
  worst_class_x: { displayName: Worst class, description: "The worst motion class's median, in multiples of that actuator's measurement floor: 1 × is as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×" }
  floor_tape_x: { displayName: Floor tape, description: "The five floor repeats, in multiples of that actuator's measurement floor: 1 × is as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×" }
  twin_grade: { displayName: Twin-grade, type: status, description: Within 1.5 × of the floor on every held-out tape, options: [{ value: "yes", color: green, group: done }, { value: "no", color: red, group: in_progress }] }
  runner_up_x: { displayName: Runner-up }
  rank_desc: { displayName: Models ranked }
  n_runs: { displayName: Runs, type: number, showAs: bar, color: blue, description: Runs behind the number (the bar against the most) }
  bench: { displayName: Bench, type: select }
  benches: { displayName: Benches, type: multi_select }
  test: { displayName: Test, type: select }
  run: { displayName: Run }
  q_rms_mrad: { displayName: q RMS }
  x_floor: { displayName: × floor, icon: target, description: "Error in multiples of that actuator's measurement floor: 1 × is as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×" }
  coulomb: { displayName: Coulomb }
  viscous: { displayName: Viscous }
  breakaway: { displayName: Breakaway }
  stribeck_velocity: { displayName: Stribeck velocity }
  weakening: { displayName: Weakening }
  capture_fraction: { displayName: Fraction, type: percent, showAs: bar, color: purple, description: Share of the load the capture term carries }
  capture_speed: { displayName: Speed }
  capture_dwell: { displayName: Dwell }
  ripple: { displayName: Ripple RMS }
  backlash: { displayName: Backlash }
  gear_stiffness: { displayName: Gear stiffness }
  inertia: { displayName: Inertia }
  torque_scale: { displayName: Torque scale }
  kt: { displayName: Kt (output) }
  current_loop: { displayName: Current loop }
  term: { displayName: Term switched off, type: select }
  delta_mrad: { displayName: Error added }
  delta_x: { displayName: Added × floor }
  term_note: { displayName: What it models }
  description: { displayName: What it is }
  readme: { displayName: README (at the fit commit) }
  code_commit: { displayName: Fitted with commit, icon: hash }
  code_path: { displayName: Code }
  code_hosted: { displayName: Hosted, icon: globe }
views:
  - type: pivot
    name: Benches
    intro:
      text: |
        **How does every model do on every bench?** A row is a model, rolled up across the actuators it ran on; a
        column is one bench test; a cell is the median error of every run behind it, in multiples of that actuator's
        measurement floor (1 × = as close as the rack repeats itself; twin-grade is ≤ 1.5 ×). In the strip, each dot
        is a run and the tall tick their median, on one scale per column (its ends in the header). **Roll up** in the
        toolbar brings the actuators back; click a cell for its runs, a model's name for its page.
      kpi:
        filters:
          and:
            - 'kind == "run"'
            - '!x_floor.isEmpty()'
        groupBy: { property: bench }
        kpi:
          value: { property: x_floor, summary: Median }
          gate: { max: 1.5 }
    filters:
      and:
        - 'kind == "run"'
        - '!x_floor.isEmpty()'
    order: [variant, actuator]
    groupBy: { property: rung, direction: ASC }
    splitBy: [bench, test]
    value: { property: x_floor, summary: Median, display: dist }
    rollup: { keep: [variant], dims: [actuator, variant, model, rung, family] }
    columnSize: { variant: 200 }
  - type: pivot
    name: Benches · every actuator
    intro:
      text: |
        The same pivot **without the roll-up**: one row per model per actuator, grouped actuator › rung, so a model's
        weak actuator shows. This is the drill-down of **Benches**; models that never ran read "—", never 0.
    filters: 'kind == "run"'
    order: [variant]
    groupBy: { property: actuator }
    subGroupBy: { property: rung, direction: ASC }
    splitBy: [bench]
    value: { property: x_floor, summary: Median, display: dist }
  - type: table
    name: Leaderboard
    intro:
      text: |
        **Which model wins on each actuator, and is it twin-grade yet?** A card is an actuator's best model on the
        Oct 23 held-out tapes (× its floor), the delta its lead over the runner-up, the gate twin-grade's 1.5 ×, the
        spark its models worst → best. Below, every model ranked, **rolled up across actuators** (a cell's dots are the
        actuators it ran on); un-roll in **Roll up**, click a row for the actuators behind it.
      kpi:
        filters:
          and:
            - 'kind == "model"'
            - '!headline_x.isEmpty()'
        groupBy: { property: leader }
        kpi:
          value: { property: headline_x }
          compare: { against: runner_up_x, better: lower, neutral: 0.02 }
          spark: { x: rank_desc, y: headline_x }
          gate: { max: 1.5 }
    filters:
      and:
        - 'kind == "model"'
        - '!headline_x.isEmpty()'
    order: [variant, rung, headline_x, actuator, dataset_x, worst_class_x, floor_tape_x, twin_grade, n_runs]
    sort:
      - { property: headline_x, direction: ASC }
    display: { headline_x: dist }
    rollup: { keep: [variant], dims: [actuator, variant, model, ladder_step, rung, family] }
    record:
      sections:
        - { name: Model, properties: [variant, actuator, rung, family, description] }
        - { name: Error, properties: [headline_x, dataset_x, worst_class_x, floor_tape_x, twin_grade, benches] }
        - { name: Code, properties: [code_commit, code_hosted, code_path, readme] }
  - type: chart
    name: Rung ladder
    filters:
      and:
        - 'kind == "model"'
        - '!headline_x.isEmpty()'
    chart:
      mark: { type: line, point: true }
      encoding:
        x: { field: ladder_step, title: "the model ladder, simplest first" }
        y: { field: headline_x, scale: { type: log }, title: "held-out error (× floor)" }
        color: { field: actuator }
    guides:
      - { rule: { y: 1.5 }, label: "twin-grade ≤ 1.5 × floor" }
    hover: { title: variant, fields: [actuator, headline_x, headline_mrad, twin_grade] }
  - type: table
    name: Parameters
    intro:
      text: |
        **What does each model run on?** One row per model and actuator with the terms it was fitted with, grouped
        under Friction, Capture, Drivetrain and Driver. The mark after a value is its basis (● measured, ○ an estimate
        whose fit the model card refused, C chosen); hover a value for its 95 % CI and source. "—" is a term the model
        does not run, with the reason on hover. The cards are each actuator's Coulomb friction in its best model.
      kpi:
        filters:
          and:
            - 'kind == "model"'
            - 'best == true'
        groupBy: { property: actuator }
        kpi:
          value: { property: coulomb }
    filters: 'kind == "model"'
    order: [variant, actuator, coulomb, viscous, breakaway, stribeck_velocity, weakening, capture_fraction, capture_speed, capture_dwell, ripple, backlash, gear_stiffness, inertia, kt, current_loop, torque_scale]
    groupBy: { property: rung }
    groupOrder: [M2, M3, M4, M5, M1, M0]
    columnGroups:
      Friction: [coulomb, viscous, breakaway, stribeck_velocity, weakening]
      Capture: [capture_fraction, capture_speed, capture_dwell]
      Drivetrain: [ripple, backlash, gear_stiffness, inertia]
      Driver: [kt, current_loop, torque_scale]
    display: { coulomb: value, viscous: value, weakening: value, ripple: value, backlash: value, inertia: value, kt: value }
    record:
      sections:
        - { name: Model, properties: [variant, actuator, rung, description] }
        - { name: Terms, properties: [coulomb, viscous, weakening, ripple, backlash, inertia, kt, current_loop] }
        - { name: Code, properties: [code_commit, code_hosted, code_path, readme] }
  - type: table
    name: Parameters · with CI
    intro:
      text: |
        The friction terms **split into sub-columns**: value, the 95 % CI's low and high, and the basis, each its own
        column under its term, instead of the range squeezed into the cell.
    filters:
      and:
        - 'kind == "model"'
        - '!coulomb.isEmpty()'
    order: [variant, actuator, coulomb, viscous, weakening]
    groupBy: { property: rung, direction: ASC }
    display: { coulomb: stats, viscous: stats, weakening: stats }
    stats:
      coulomb: { parts: [value, low, high, basis], labels: { low: 95% CI low, high: high } }
      viscous: { parts: [value, low, high, basis], labels: { low: 95% CI low, high: high } }
      weakening: { parts: [value, low, high, basis], labels: { low: 95% CI low, high: high } }
  - type: table
    name: What each rung adds
    intro:
      text: |
        **What does each term buy?** The full twin's ablation: switch one term off and replay the held-out tapes; the
        error added is how much worse the twin gets (positive = the term helps). The strip shows every run's change on
        one scale per column (dots runs, tall tick their median). The cards: the median added per rung, across actuators.
      kpi:
        filters: 'kind == "term"'
        groupBy: { property: rung }
        kpi:
          value: { property: delta_x, summary: Median }
    filters: 'kind == "term"'
    order: [term, actuator, delta_mrad, delta_x, term_note]
    groupBy: { property: rung }
    groupOrder: [M2, M3, M4, driver]
    sort:
      - { property: delta_x, direction: DESC }
    summaries: { delta_x: Median }
    display: { delta_mrad: dist }
  - type: table
    name: What each rung adds · columns
    intro:
      text: |
        The same ablation with the distribution **as columns**: the median, min and max of the per-run change, how many
        runs, and the strip, each under "Error added".
    filters: 'kind == "term"'
    order: [term, actuator, delta_mrad, delta_x]
    groupBy: { property: rung }
    groupOrder: [M2, M3, M4, driver]
    sort:
      - { property: delta_x, direction: DESC }
    display: { delta_mrad: stats }
  - type: table
    name: Runs
    filters: 'kind == "run"'
    order: [variant, bench, test, run, q_rms_mrad, x_floor]
    groupBy: { property: actuator }
    subGroupBy: { property: variant }
    sort:
      - { property: x_floor, direction: ASC }
    summaries: { q_rms_mrad: Median, x_floor: Median }
    fold: closed
